EXT. HIGHWAY 9 UNDERPASS - DAY

A white delivery van reading "SWEET NOTHINGS BAKERY" sits wedged under a concrete overpass, its roof crushed against the girders. Traffic backs up for a mile. Horns.

BARTEK LISOWSKI, 50s, driver, round and sweating, stands on the bumper inspecting the roof with the dignity of a surgeon. His assistant JULES, 22, nose ring, apron over a hoodie, holds a phone to her ear and a clipboard to her chest. The back doors are open. Inside, a seven-tier wedding cake, miraculously upright, trembles with every honk.

JULES
(into the phone)
Pen, we're fine. We're almost there.

PENELOPE (V.O.)
(phone)
The ceremony is in twenty minutes.

JULES
Yes. Yes. I know.

BARTEK
(to himself)
Twelve feet two. The sign said twelve feet six.

JULES
(covering the phone)
Bartek, the sign was for the other bridge.

BARTEK
There is only one bridge.

JULES
There are two. We took the wrong one.

PENELOPE (V.O.)
(phone)
Jules, what was that?

JULES
Nothing! A bird!

BARTEK
(to the traffic)
Please! Please! A little patience!

A horn answers him. Then another. He mops his forehead.

BARTEK (CONT'D)
(to Jules)
Let the air out of the tires.

JULES
The tires?

BARTEK
It lowers the van. An inch. Maybe two.

PENELOPE (V.O.)
(phone)
Jules, I can hear honking. Where are you?

JULES
It's a parade.

PENELOPE (V.O.)
On a Saturday morning?

JULES
It's a very Saturday parade.

Bartek kneels. Unscrews a valve. Hiss. The van sinks half an inch, then stops. The cake sways. Jules gasps. Bartek holds up one palm like a conductor.

BARTEK
Steady. Steady.

The cake settles. A man in the next car leans on his horn.

BARTEK (CONT'D)
(whisper)
I will end him.

JULES
Bartek!

BARTEK
Pardon. A joke.

PENELOPE (V.O.)
(phone, sharp)
Jules. Are you at the church, or are you not at the church?

JULES
Pen, we will be at the church. I swear.

Bartek unscrews the second valve. The van sinks another inch. The roof shrieks off the girder. The van rolls free. The cake lurches. Jules shrieks. Bartek, arms wide, stands in the road in front of the van as if he could catch the cake with his body.

It stays. All three seconds of silence are enormous.

BARTEK (CONT'D)
(to the traffic, hoarse)
You may go now.

Horns erupt, joyfully.
